        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 过节",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "过节 — guòjié — \"to celebrate a festival\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "去年我们回老家过节 qùnián wǒmen huí lǎojiā guòjié — Last year we went back to our home town for the festival."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "过节 (guòjié) is built from 过 'to pass' and 节 'a festival', both inherited from Middle Chinese, kwaH and tset (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to go beyond' and the second 'a joint of bamboo'. The sense 'a festival' is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
